@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<div class="container py-4">
    <div class="text-center mb-4">
        <h1 class="display-4">@ViewData["Title"]</h1>
        <p class="lead">How we collect, use, and protect personal information in the Leave Management System.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Introduction</h2>
        <p>
            This Privacy Policy explains how Leave Management System ("we", "us", "the system") collects,
            uses, stores, and shares personal information when you use our service to request or manage employee leave.
            We are committed to protecting the privacy of employees, managers, and administrators who use the system.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account & Profile:</strong> name, work email, employee ID, job title, manager, department.</li>
            <li><strong>Leave Records:</strong> leave type, start/end dates, reason (if provided), approval history, attachments (e.g., medical certificates).</li>
            <li><strong>Employment Data:</strong> hire date, work schedule, leave balances and history required to calculate entitlements.</li>
            <li><strong>Usage & System Data:</strong> IP address, device/browser information, timestamps for sign-ins and actions, audit logs.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Process leave requests, approvals, cancellations and to update leave balances.</li>
            <li>Communicate with employees and managers about requests and policy changes.</li>
            <li>Support payroll and HR reporting when authorized by your employer.</li>
            <li>Maintain security, perform troubleshooting and generate usage and compliance reports.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Legal Basis</h2>
        <p>
            Where applicable (for example under data protection laws), we process personal data on the legal bases
            necessary for performance of contracts with your employer, to comply with legal obligations, or for our
            legitimate business interests (such as providing, securing and improving the service).
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Sharing & Disclosure</h2>
        <p>We may share personal information with:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Your employer's HR and payroll systems when required to administer leave and pay.</li>
            <li>Authorized managers and administrators within your organization to process and approve leave.</li>
            <li>Service providers who host, maintain or process data for the system under contract and confidentiality obligations.</li>
            <li>When required by law, regulation, or to respond to legal requests or protect rights and safety.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
            We retain personal information for as long as necessary to provide the service to your employer and to
            meet legal, accounting or reporting requirements. Retention periods may be determined by your employer's
            data retention policy.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>
            We implement reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect personal data against
            accidental or unlawful destruction, loss, alteration, unauthorized disclosure or access. However, no
            system is completely secure — if you suspect a security issue, notify your administrator immediately.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Your Rights</h2>
        <p>
            Depending on your jurisdiction and role, you may have rights to access, correct, export, or request
            deletion of your personal information. Requests should be made to your employer's HR department or
            the contact listed below; we will cooperate to the extent permitted by law and contractual obligations.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Cookies & Tracking</h2>
        <p>
            We use cookies and similar technologies for session management, authentication, analytics and to
            improve the user experience. You can control cookie settings in your browser; disabling some cookies
            may affect system functionality.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>International Transfers</h2>
        <p>
            Personal data may be processed or stored outside your country. When we transfer data internationally,
            we use appropriate safeguards such as standard contractual clauses or rely on approved legal mechanisms.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or wish to exercise your rights, contact your employer's
            HR team or email the system administrator at <a href="mailto:privacy@yourcompany.example">privacy@yourcompany.example</a>.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-3">
        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time. When significant changes occur, we will provide notice
            through the system or via your employer. This policy is effective as of the date shown below.
        </p>
        <p class="text-muted">Effective date: 2026-01-01</p>
    </section>
</div>
